WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.731
Every request to Telo Ride needs a signed-in rider, unless it is on a short, written

00:00:07.731 --> 00:00:08.338
list.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.946
The list: sign-in and sign-out, the public class and map catalogues, the health

00:00:14.946 --> 00:00:19.458
checks, and the app itself. Each is marked anonymous where it is mapped.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:29.353
Everything else answers 401 without a session, as ProblemDetails, never a redirect.

00:00:33.552 --> 00:00:38.990
A new test asks every endpoint the API maps, the ride hub included. Mark rides

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.730
anonymous by mistake, and it fails.

00:00:46.457 --> 00:00:51.671
A change must also come from Telo Ride itself. The browser marks where each request

00:00:51.671 --> 00:00:54.861
came from, and a page cannot change that mark.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:05.226
A change from another site is refused with 403, cross origin, before it reaches the

00:01:05.226 --> 00:01:08.141
rider's data. So is a hub connection.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.999
Riders see nothing new: sign-in still opens, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.824
Four hundred and eighty-eight backend tests pass, on a host in memory, with no real

00:01:27.824 --> 00:01:28.692
database.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:37.517
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:37.862 --> 00:01:42.373
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:42.373 --> 00:01:44.044
every hill and interval.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:49.568
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:55.016
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:55.016 --> 00:01:58.006
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.843
A custom workout lives under Profile.
